dsudo(8) -- default password sudo
=============================================

<!--
# Copyright (C) 2019 - 2025 ENCRYPTED SUPPORT LLC <adrelanos@whonix.org>
# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS
`dsudo [OPTIONS]`

## DESCRIPTION
Runs `sudo` submitting the account's default EMPTY password.

Forwards all environment variables and parameters to `sudo`.

Sets `SUDO_ASKPASS=/usr/libexec/derivative-base-files/askpass-default`
which submits `sudo_password` (default: empty, matching the empty
password Kicksecure accounts ship with) - unless environment variable
`sudo_password` is already set to something else (e.g.
`sudo_password=changeme dsudo ...` for a legacy image).

Useful for headless/automated root (no tty), where a plain `sudo -n`
is refused because an empty password still has to be submitted.

